2:id: lem-homeomorphism-criteria
4:title: "A continuous bijection is a homeomorphism iff it is open iff it is closed, and homeomorphy is an equivalence relation on spaces"
35:## Statement
36:
37:Let $X$ and $Y$ be topological spaces.
38:
39:1. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a continuous bijection
40:   ([[def-continuous-map-top]], [[def-homeomorphism-and-open-maps]]). The
41:   following are equivalent:
42:   - (a) $f$ is a homeomorphism;
43:   - (b) $f$ is an open map;
44:   - (c) $f$ is a closed map.
45:2. Homeomorphy is an equivalence relation: $X \cong X$; if $X \cong Y$ then
46:   $Y \cong X$; and if $X \cong Y$ and $Y \cong Z$ then $X \cong Z$.
47:
48:Continuity is a genuine hypothesis in claim 1: a bijection that is open and
49:closed but not continuous exists as soon as two comparable topologies differ, for
50:instance the identity from the coarser to the finer of two distinct topologies on
51:one set.
