2:id: thm-continuity-characterisations-top
4:title: "For a map of spaces the following agree: continuity at every point, preimages of open sets open, preimages of closed sets closed, preimages of subbasic open sets open, and $f(\\overline{A}) \\subseteq \\overline{f(A)}$"
33:## Statement
34:
35:Let $(X, \mathcal{T}_X)$ and $(Y, \mathcal{T}_Y)$ be topological spaces, let
36:$f : X \to Y$ be a function, and let $\mathcal{S}$ be a subbasis for
37:$\mathcal{T}_Y$ ([[def-topology-basis-subbasis]]). The following five conditions
38:are equivalent.
39:
40:- **(a)** $f$ is continuous at every point of $X$ ([[def-continuous-map-top]]).
41:- **(b)** $f^{-1}[V]$ is open in $X$ for every open $V \subseteq Y$.
42:- **(c)** $f^{-1}[F]$ is closed in $X$ for every closed $F \subseteq Y$.
43:- **(d)** $f^{-1}[S]$ is open in $X$ for every $S \in \mathcal{S}$.
44:- **(e)** $f[\overline{A}] \subseteq \overline{f[A]}$ for every $A \subseteq X$,
45:  closures being taken in $X$ and in $Y$ respectively
46:  ([[def-interior-closure-boundary-top]]).
47:
48:Condition (d) is what makes continuity checkable against a generating family
49:rather than against every open set, and it holds for a *basis* as well, a basis
50:being in particular a subbasis for the topology it generates.
