35:## Statement
36:
37:**Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]) and the Axiom
38:of Dependent Choice ([[def-dependent-choice]]).** Let $(X,d)$ be a metric space
39:([[def-metric-space]]). Then the following five conditions are equivalent.
40:
41:- **(a)** $(X,d)$ is compact ([[def-metric-compactness]]).
42:- **(b)** $(X,d)$ is countably compact ([[def-metric-compactness-variants]]).
43:- **(c)** $(X,d)$ is limit point compact.
44:- **(d)** $(X,d)$ is sequentially compact.
45:- **(e)** $(X,d)$ is complete ([[def-complete-metric-space]]) and totally bounded
46:  ([[def-totally-bounded]]).
47:
48:**The two hypotheses are not needed everywhere, and the statement should not be
